go 1.26.0

// Every module in the repository, so that a change spanning two of them is one
// change: built together, tested together, committed together. That is the whole
// reason to keep them in one repository rather than five, and it is why this file
// is committed rather than ignored — without it a checkout does not build.
//
// The repository root is not one of them. A module is a unit of distribution and
// the root distributes nothing: a module there would be an empty thing to tag, an
// empty page on pkg.go.dev, and a question every reader has to ask. The tests that
// guard the layering live in ./internal, which is a module because it has to be
// compiled to run and not because anyone will ever depend on it.
use (
	./components
	./core
	./examples
	./internal
	./ptytest
)
